  "exhibits": [
    {
      "id": "isc-m2-tbs5-ex1",
      "title": "Claims",
      "html": "<p>Management maps policies to a framework and calls that proof of effectiveness. A monthly privileged-access review excludes administrators. A detective alert has no assigned responder. A sample exception is deleted because most items passed.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "isc-m2-tbs5-ex2",
      "title": "Evaluation approach",
      "html": "<p>Connect control design and actual operation to specific risks, objectives, evidence, and exception follow-up.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "<h3>Framework-mapping conclusion</h3><p>Framework alignment is an organizing step, not operating evidence.</p><h3>Access-review design concern</h3><p>Administrators are central to the privileged-access objective.</p><h3>Alert-response weakness</h3><p>Detection needs an actionable response process.</p><h3>Appropriate exception treatment</h3><p>Exceptions must remain part of the evidence evaluation.</p>"
